{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed single storey infill extension by reason of its scale and positioning in conjunction with the depth of the proposed rear extension existing two storey and its siting close to&amp;nbsp; the shared boundary with No.13 Grant Road, would be unduly obtrusive, result in loss of light, overshadowing, sense of enclosure and would be detrimental to the residential amenities of the occupiers of the adjoining property no. 13 Grant Road, contrary to Policy D3.D (1) and (11) of The London Plan (2021),&amp;nbsp; Core Policy CS1B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; line-height: 107%; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;The proposed, by reason of its shortfall in the\r\ngross internal floor areas, poor outlook from a habitable space, poor design\r\nwith the insertion of rooflights in the single storey extension on the rear\r\nelevation, would result in loss of privacy for future occupiers of Flat A and poor\r\nstandard of living accommodation for future occupiers of Flat B, to the\r\ndetriment of their residential amenities contrary to the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework (2024), Policies D3 and D6 of The London Plan (2021), Policies\r\nDM1 and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), The\r\nMayor of London: London Plan Guidance - Housing Design Standards (2023) and the\r\nadopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
